/*
TRALLALLA AUDIO HANDOVER — approved setup, 26 October 2026, v1.8.0
================================================================
The owner explicitly approved these voices. Preserve their existing recordings;
append new clips, rather than replacing the bank or changing engines globally.
This HTML is the complete distributable. Build tools below are developer-only.

VOICE CAST
  ru-svetlana: Microsoft ru-RU-SvetlanaNeural, female Russian guide/characters.
  ru-eugene:   Silero v5.6, speaker eugene, male Russian characters.
  it-isabella:Microsoft it-IT-IsabellaNeural, female Italian guide/reactions.
  it-diego:   Microsoft it-IT-DiegoNeural, male Italian reactions.
  Explicit character gender wins over guide preference in automatic cast mode.
  Forced female/male preferences are respected. Never guess a device fallback.
  Microsoft voices are service-generated recordings, not open-source models.
  Engine provenance: github.com/rany2/edge-tts; github.com/snakers4/silero-models.

KNOWN WORKING BUILD ENVIRONMENT
  Python 3.12; edge-tts 7.3.1; NumPy 2.5.4; FFmpeg 8.0.
  Russian male build also uses PyTorch 2.14.1+cpu and official Silero v5_6_ru.pt.
  None of these dependencies is loaded by the game, and no API key is in the file.

PROSODY AND DSP — preserve these before trying new tuning
  Edge ordinary speech: -5% rate; <=5 alphanumeric characters: -14% rate.
  Russian alphabet: synthesize the letter NAME, not a raw consonant; Edge -30%.
  Positive quick/perfect/streak reactions: +7% rate, +3Hz pitch AT GENERATION.
  Level completion/recovery reactions: +2% rate, +3Hz at generation.
  Silero eugene: 48000Hz model synthesis; automatic stress/yo for full words;
  for letter names disable auto accent/yo and stress_single_vowel. Isolated ё
  trips the model's text-presence check: synthesize йо for that letter name.
  Base time stretch for Silero: .97 ordinary, .91 short, .78 alphabet;
  Edge alphabet uses .86. All time stretch is pitch-preserving FFmpeg atempo.
  Decode to mono float PCM 24000Hz. Find active samples above abs(.0025).
  Keep 30ms BEFORE and 60ms AFTER active speech; do not clip final consonants.
  Normalize the peak to .86. Alphabet active span target >=.56s; short words
  >=.42s. Limit extra stretching to 2x so a damaged clip is caught, not hidden.
  Add 45ms leading silence and 170ms tail for alphabet, 90ms tail otherwise.
  Export MP3, mono, 24000Hz, 48kbit/s. Listen to new clips before distribution.
  For slower lessons create a second file with atempo=.8. Never implement slow
  playback by changing WebAudio playbackRate: that changes the approved timbre.

BANK CONTRACT
  TR_NEURAL_PACK.clips[voiceId][normalizedText] = MP3 base64 (no data URI prefix).
  meta[voiceId][key].kind is letter / short / speech / reaction.
  slow[voiceId][key] is the pitch-preserving .8x recording for teaching material.
  Reaction clips do not need slow variants. reactions[group] lists exact captions.
  Reward pools route to Italian voices; store Russian examples as teaching speech
  unless implementing explicit language routing for rewards first.
  Key normalization must match trNeuralNorm/trCleanSpeechText: strip tags/entities,
  accent U+0301 and angle quotes; replace hyphens/slashes with spaces; NFC, lower,
  collapse whitespace and remove trailing punctuation. Aa-style Cyrillic pairs
  collapse to their single letter key. Reuse existing keys/bytes when available.

EVENT AND MIXER CONTRACT — do not break the learning flow
  A validated correct match/answer/photo/finished word calls trFeedback ONCE.
  A mistake calls trResetStreak. Navigation cancels pending reactions.
  Milestones: 3,5,8,12; beyond 12 every fourth success uses non-numeric audio.
  Numeric voice lines must agree with the event's immutable streak snapshot.
  Shuffle bags and a six-caption history prevent immediate repetition.
  Bigger pending milestones outrank routine praise; the latest larger streak wins.
  Learning speech has first priority. Reaction speech waits for narration AND
  active reaction speech to finish, plus 160ms quiet. Never queue a long backlog.
  User-triggered listening stops active praise immediately. Hidden pages cancel it.
  Use the shared voice/music/fx mixer, never new Audio() or speechSynthesis for a
  built-in clip. Resuming AudioContext remains synchronous in the pointer gesture.
  Music ducks to 8% and effects to 6% of their configured levels during teaching
  speech; reaction speech temporarily ducks music to 30%. Preserve separate mutes.
  All WebAudio voice sources run at playbackRate=1. Existing slow assets do the work.

SATISFACTION CONTRACT
  Each reward has one event id, caption, voice, tier and immutable streak count.
  Visual feedback appears immediately; a short visual glint/echo accompanies the
  actual voice start if narration delayed it. Never display a different streak.
  The wow layer and all descendants are pointer-events:none, have no focus trap,
  and never delay Next/shutter/input or alter board/camera geometry.
  Only one transient reward layer exists; particles are capped at 32. Clear on
  navigation/hidden state. Respect visuals toggle, sound preferences and reduced
  motion: keep readable success text, remove spatial/light/particle motion.
  The portable Python append-tool is kept below as TR_AUDIO_BUILD_RECIPE.

RELEASE CHECKS
  Fingerprint the existing clips + slow maps and assert byte-for-byte preservation.
  Decode every added clip; reject empty/silent audio. Check isolated letters and
  short words, a long mixed-language explanation, voice casting, touch start/stop,
  muted/reduced-motion paths, rapid streaks, wrong-answer reset, navigation cancel,
  and end-level perfect/recovery. Tests must not wait for a flourish to advance.
  Update TR_VERSION, application-version meta and the public in-app changelog.
  Do not ship external models, loose audio, CDN calls, keys, or helper files.
*/
const TR_AUDIO_AUTHORING=Object.freeze({schema:1,approvedSetup:'2026-10-26',voiceIds:['ru-svetlana','ru-eugene','it-isabella','it-diego'],sampleRate:24000,channels:1,codec:'mp3',bitrate:48000,peak:.86,activeThreshold:.0025,preSpeechMs:30,postSpeechMs:60,leadingMs:45,tailMs:{letter:170,speech:90},minimumActiveSeconds:{letter:.56,short:.42},slowTempo:.8,sourcePlaybackRate:1,reactionProsody:{quick:{rate:'+7%',pitch:'+3Hz'},completion:{rate:'+2%',pitch:'+3Hz'}},streaks:[3,5,8,12],beyondStreakEvery:4,maxParticles:32,maxRewardLayers:1,voicePriority:'teaching > reaction > music/fx'});

